Allow the fast transcription model (qwen/qwen3.8-flash) on every plan, so the app's fast reading of a clicked
question runs on the model it asks for instead of falling back to Haiku. Apply in the backend repository (the
Worker), then deploy. Nothing else changes: the model is only used when the app asks for it by name, without the
X-LearnLayer-Area / Route headers.

--- a/backend/src/config.ts
+++ b/backend/src/config.ts
@@
 export const DEEPSEEK = "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash";
+/** The fast reading of a clicked question's picture (FastTranscription): the app asks it by name. */
+export const QWEN_FAST = "qwen/qwen3.8-flash";
 export const SPEECH_TURBO = "elevenlabs/eleven-v4-turbo";
@@ free
-        chatModels: [HAIKU, GEMINI, DEEPSEEK],
+        chatModels: [HAIKU, GEMINI, DEEPSEEK, QWEN_FAST],
@@ plus
